 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 9.56,
   "text": "the worst planet ever discovered. Glass rain, winds faster than sound, 1000 degrees,"
  },
  {
   "start": 10.34,
   "end": 16.58,
   "text": "and it smells like rotten eggs. Welcome to the worst planet ever discovered."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.08,
   "end": 23.42,
   "text": "Its name is HD 189733 b, and it is not in our solar system."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.08,
   "end": 27.3,
   "text": "Our sun is just one of billions of stars in our galaxy."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.86,
   "end": 33.42,
   "text": "Many of those stars have planets of their own. Scientists call them exoplanets. So far,"
  },
  {
   "start": 33.66,
   "end": 38.74,
   "text": "they have found more than 6,000. But few are as terrifying as this one."
  },
  {
   "start": 39.36,
   "end": 44.36,
   "text": "This planet is about 64 light years away. So how do we know anything about it?"
  },
  {
   "start": 44.82,
   "end": 49.9,
   "text": "When the planet passes in front of its star, star light shines through its air. By studying"
  },
  {
   "start": 49.9,
   "end": 55.28,
   "text": "that light, scientists can tell what the planet is made of. And what they found was shocking."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.92,
   "end": 61.8,
   "text": "From far away, the planet looks deep blue, just like Earth. But it has no oceans."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.64,
   "end": 67.02,
   "text": "Scientists think the blue color may come from tiny bits of glass floating in its clouds."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.76,
   "end": 71.02,
   "text": "Glass is made from silica, the same material found in sand."
  },
  {
   "start": 71.64,
   "end": 77.42,
   "text": "This planet is a giant, bigger than Jupiter, and it sits extremely close to its star."
  },
  {
   "start": 77.94,
   "end": 80.84,
   "text": "One year there lasts only about two Earth days."
  },
  {
   "start": 80.84,
   "end": 86.84,
   "text": "The temperature can reach around 1,000 degrees Celsius, hot enough to melt many metals."
  },
  {
   "start": 87.56,
   "end": 93.3,
   "text": "One side always faces its star, so it is always day. The other side is always night."
  },
  {
   "start": 93.88,
   "end": 97.12,
   "text": "That huge difference in heat creates monstrous winds,"
  },
  {
   "start": 97.66,
   "end": 101.14,
   "text": "thousands of kilometers per hour, faster than the speed of sound."
  },
  {
   "start": 101.66,
   "end": 107.88,
   "text": "Now put it all together. Glass in the clouds, winds faster than sound. Scientists think this"
  },
  {
   "start": 107.88,
   "end": 113.92,
   "text": "could create rain made of glass, flying sideways. Standing there would be like being hit by millions"
  },
  {
   "start": 113.92,
   "end": 121.28,
   "text": "of tiny blades. And the rotten egg smell? In 2024, the James Webb Space Telescope found a gas called"
  },
  {
   "start": 121.28,
   "end": 126.46,
   "text": "hydrogen sulfide on this planet. On Earth, that's the gas that smells like rotten eggs."
  },
  {
   "start": 127.0,
   "end": 133.46,
   "text": "But remember, nobody has actually seen glass rain there. It is a scientific idea based on telescope"
  },
  {
   "start": 133.46,
   "end": 139.62,
   "text": "data, and scientists are still studying it. From far away, it looks like a peaceful blue marble."
  },
  {
   "start": 140.18,
   "end": 146.5,
   "text": "Up close, it may be one of the deadliest places we know. It makes you realize how special our"
  },
  {
   "start": 146.5,
   "end": 154.62,
   "text": "own blue planet is. Soft rain, fresh air, life everywhere. Out there, among thousands of worlds,"
  },
  {
   "start": 154.9,
   "end": 160.28,
   "text": "we have not found another place like home. And here's the thing. Billions of planets,"
  },
  {
   "start": 160.28,
   "end": 167.2,
   "text": "and not one of them can care. But you can. Don't ever forget how special that makes you."
  },
  {
   "start": 167.92,
   "end": 172.18,
   "text": "Space is truly amazing. And this is only the beginning."
  }
 ]
}